  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 246 AM CDT Sat Oct 17 2026\n\nFrost/freeze headlines remain intact through 9 AM across much of the \narea. High pressure at the surface will translate eastward into the \nMiddle Mississippi Valley area today allowing southerly winds to \nreturn to the region. Breezy southerly winds will develop over much \nof the area on Sunday while persisting through early next week. This \nwill result in rising temperatures with seasonable values \nanticipated early in the week while above average values arrive as\nwe head into the middle and latter portion of the week. \nSoutherly winds will gradually allow some low level moisture to \nreturn to the region but it will be slow to arrive, limiting any\nmeaningful chances for wetting precipitation. A shortwave \ntrough may emerge from the Rockies as we move into the weekend \nbringing increasing probabilities for showers late Fri into Sat.\nOtherwise, dry and mild conditions are expected through much of\nthe upcoming week.",
